WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.324 --> 00:00:09.287
It was a beautiful day in First City, and the streets buzzed with energy.

2
00:00:09.347 --> 00:00:37.397
At the edge of Treeview the king and queen of Magica were speaking to a large gathering.

3
00:00:38.578 --> 00:00:40.859
Angry people held banners and signs.

4
00:00:42.059 --> 00:00:46.481
Some signs were magical, with flashing messages that changed words or colors.

5
00:00:47.522 --> 00:00:49.482
Others were plain signs written by hand.

6
00:00:50.523 --> 00:00:55.705
There had been many protests lately, and now the king and queen were trying to calm down the

7
00:00:55.725 --> 00:01:02.908
crowd. A square-jawed man watched from a balcony overlooking the park.

8
00:01:04.128 --> 00:01:09.630
His big hands rested on a railing, and a door behind him was open to an opulent apartment.

9
00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:11.890
"Void rights," he muttered.

10
00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:13.671
"What a concept.

11
00:01:14.371 --> 00:01:15.351
Seems popular though."

12
00:01:16.311 --> 00:01:21.433
Suddenly he gasped, his knees buckling as his head exploded with pain.

13
00:01:22.473 --> 00:01:27.394
Pressing his hands to his head, he staggered through the door and collapsed onto a sofa.

14
00:01:28.575 --> 00:01:32.716
A moment later the pain faded, and his eyes opened wide with surprise.

15
00:01:33.856 --> 00:01:35.157
"Who is this?"

16
00:01:35.537 --> 00:01:36.157
he exclaimed.

17
00:01:36.177 --> 00:01:38.298
"How are you—?"

18
00:01:39.398 --> 00:01:42.480
He paused, listening to a voice only he could hear.

19
00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:44.380
Then he nodded.

20
00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:47.822
"Yes, of course I remember you.

21
00:01:48.702 --> 00:01:49.342
Who could forget?"

22
00:01:50.003 --> 00:01:52.024
He barked out a short, humorless laugh.

23
00:01:52.044 --> 00:01:54.004
"But I thought you were dead!

24
00:01:55.265 --> 00:02:00.547
That crazy old woman told the palace that she was going to His words trailed off and he

25
00:02:00.607 --> 00:02:02.228
cocked his head, listening again.

26
00:02:03.392 --> 00:02:05.693
"Yes, I see," he said.

27
00:02:05.713 --> 00:02:08.254
"Well, I'm glad.

28
00:02:09.174 --> 00:02:10.155
I've missed your business.

29
00:02:11.015 --> 00:02:11.976
But where are you now?"

30
00:02:13.176 --> 00:02:17.298
A loud cheer rose from the gathering below, but the man hardly heard it.

31
00:02:18.358 --> 00:02:20.419
The voice in his head was speaking again.

32
00:02:20.439 --> 00:02:24.161
"Who? Oh," the man said.

33
00:02:24.181 --> 00:02:26.262
"Yes, I can do that."

34
00:02:27.102 --> 00:02:29.023
This time when he listened, he frowned.

35
00:02:29.963 --> 00:02:31.924
He rose to his feet and began pacing.

36
00:02:33.764 --> 00:02:34.705
"I never fail!"

37
00:02:34.945 --> 00:02:35.445
he snapped.

38
00:02:35.465 --> 00:02:40.389
"Never! Besides, I know the perfect person to help us."

39
00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:43.151
Another brief pause followed.

40
00:02:44.212 --> 00:02:45.933
"Of course I know who is trustworthy.

41
00:02:47.134 --> 00:02:50.136
If you doubt my judgment, perhaps you should find someone else!"

42
00:02:51.357 --> 00:02:55.059
He listened again, his mouth curving into a slight smile.

43
00:02:56.681 --> 00:02:58.122
Finally he nodded.

44
00:02:58.142 --> 00:03:01.264
"Yes, I'm glad you see that."

45
00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:05.322
He wandered back onto the balcony and glanced at the scene below.

46
00:03:09.284 --> 00:03:09.664
a deal.

47
00:03:10.365 --> 00:03:12.206
We shall make them all pay!"

48
00:03:13.146 --> 00:03:15.167
He laughed along with the voice in his head.

49
00:03:15.187 --> 00:03:18.049
"I'll begin immediately."

50
00:03:28.255 --> 00:03:30.196
you tomorrow, Zann," someone called.

51
00:03:31.164 --> 00:03:34.846
Zann waved without looking to see who'd spoken, and then stepped outside.

52
00:03:36.506 --> 00:03:40.308
After two months at First City Academy, he knew most of the kids' names.

53
00:03:41.428 --> 00:03:43.990
But he still didn't feel as if he had true friends.

54
00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:48.231
"Not like back home in Swamp Bottom," he thought.

55
00:03:49.352 --> 00:03:53.754
Zann grimaced, reminding himself that Swamp Bottom wasn't "home" anymore.

56
00:03:54.954 --> 00:04:00.992
Rubbing his fingers together, he stepped away from the building and muttered, "Zap!"

57
00:04:01.012 --> 00:04:02.913
Splash! Zann looked around.

58
00:04:04.054 --> 00:04:06.274
He was standing in a neighbor's decorative fountain.

59
00:04:06.294 --> 00:04:08.656
"Drat," Zann said.

60
00:04:09.656 --> 00:04:11.777
The neighbor was picking flutter flowers nearby.

61
00:04:11.797 --> 00:04:14.458
"Sorry," Zann said to her.

62
00:04:15.538 --> 00:04:18.860
She looked irritated for a second before her expression changed.

63
00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:22.261
"Oh, it's young Zann, the hero!"

64
00:04:22.541 --> 00:04:23.182
she exclaimed.

65
00:04:23.202 --> 00:04:25.043
"How are you?

66
00:04:25.143 --> 00:04:27.964
And how are those worlds-traveling parents of yours?"

67
00:04:29.184 --> 00:04:31.246
"Fine, thanks," Zann said politely.

68
00:04:32.286 --> 00:04:33.928
"Excuse me, I have to go."

69
00:04:35.088 --> 00:04:37.971
It still felt strange when people treated him like a celebrity.

70
00:04:38.931 --> 00:04:41.693
Months had passed, but it still happened all the time.

71
00:04:42.774 --> 00:04:44.055
He hurried over to his house.

72
00:04:45.056 --> 00:04:47.417
When he opened the front door, Zing flew out.

73
00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:53.022
The dragon chattered and spat flames.

74
00:04:53.042 --> 00:04:56.732
"Sorry I'm late," Zann told Zing.

75
00:04:56.752 --> 00:04:59.813
"I had to stay after school for an assembly about Void rights.

76
00:05:00.953 --> 00:05:08.655
The headmaster said that we're all supposed to work at getting along— Reds, Voids, dragons Zann hadn't been

77
00:05:08.675 --> 00:05:11.036
paying much attention to the Void rights protests.

78
00:05:12.016 --> 00:05:14.197
But the assembly had made him think about Darb.

79
00:05:15.217 --> 00:05:17.458
And that made him homesick for Swamp Bottom again.

80
00:05:18.598 --> 00:05:24.000
He hadn't seen Darb for more than two months—nor their friends Perda and Gliss.

81
00:05:25.156 --> 00:05:28.537
Zing started zipping around overhead, sending flames everywhere.

82
00:05:30.117 --> 00:05:31.758
Zann conjured some dragon treats.

83
00:05:31.778 --> 00:05:36.199
"It's okay, boy," he called, tossing Zing the treats.

84
00:05:36.219 --> 00:05:39.700
"I know you've been stuck in the house all day.

85
00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:42.861
But now we can go to Palace Park and play.

86
00:05:43.881 --> 00:05:47.242
I just have to stop by the lab first to tell Mom and Dad where we're going."

87
00:05:48.162 --> 00:05:50.623
Zann considered sending his parents a message moth.

88
00:05:51.643 --> 00:05:54.324
Luckily, they'd stopped monitoring his every move.

89
00:05:55.320 --> 00:06:00.162
But for a month or so after Morb had been banished from Magica, Zann had had to check

90
00:06:00.202 --> 00:06:02.043
in with his parents all the time.

91
00:06:03.083 --> 00:06:06.205
Zann tried to grab Zing to zap them both to the lab.

92
00:06:07.145 --> 00:06:09.446
But the little dragon wouldn't hold still long enough.

93
00:06:09.466 --> 00:06:13.488
"Okay, I guess we'll walk," Zann said with a shrug.

94
00:06:15.248 --> 00:06:18.110
He headed down the street, whistling for Zing to follow.

95
00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:23.172
Zing sped past him, diving to shoot flames at a passing flip fly.

96
00:06:25.708 --> 00:06:30.610
"Hey!" A man cried, jumping aside as the flames missed the fly and almost hit him.

97
00:06:30.630 --> 00:06:34.592
"Oops," Zann called and grabbed Zing by the wing.

98
00:06:34.612 --> 00:06:37.553
"Come on, little buddy, let's take the quick way."

99
00:06:39.234 --> 00:06:43.756
Zap! They landed across the street from the lab where Zann's parents worked.

100
00:06:44.776 --> 00:06:49.798
Zing yanked free immediately, diving down to attack a wiggle weed growing out of a crack in the

101
00:06:49.858 --> 00:06:53.340
sidewalk. Zann hardly noticed.

102
00:06:54.496 --> 00:06:56.697
He stared at a group of about a dozen people.

103
00:06:57.777 --> 00:07:01.239
They were marching around in front of him holding a Void rights banner.

104
00:07:02.359 --> 00:07:04.981
Several people stood nearby and watched the marchers.

105
00:07:05.001 --> 00:07:07.982
"Not another protest!"

106
00:07:08.422 --> 00:07:09.983
Zann muttered, shaking his head.

107
00:07:11.163 --> 00:07:14.445
He forgot about that when he saw a message moth fluttering toward him.

108
00:07:15.705 --> 00:07:16.606
Zing saw it too.

109
00:07:16.626 --> 00:07:18.686
"Zing, stop!"

110
00:07:18.967 --> 00:07:21.748
Zann grabbed the moth before the dragon could incinerate it.

111
00:07:24.284 --> 00:07:27.709
Zann smiled when he spotted several names scrawled on one wing.

112
00:07:28.691 --> 00:07:31.074
The moth had come from his friends in Swamp Bottom!

113
00:07:32.115 --> 00:07:35.079
Before he could read their message, he heard a shout of anger.

114
00:07:35.099 --> 00:07:37.984
"Give that back, you fire-breathing thief!"
